.TH "REMOTEPLAYBACK.DISCONNECT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RemotePlayback.disconnect_event \- RemotePlayback: disconnect event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]disconnect\f[B]\f[R] event of the
\f[CR]RemotePlayback\f[R] interface fires when the user agent
disconnects from the remote device.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqdisconnect\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
ondisconnect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLE
In the following example the value of \f[CR]RemotePlayback.state\f[R] is
printed to the console when the user agent disconnects from the remote
device.
.IP
.EX
RemotePlayback.ondisconnect = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(RemotePlayback.state);
};
.EE
